---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PersonCard from '../components/PersonCard.astro';
import { team } from '../data/team';

const creators = team.filter((person) => person.org === 'Program Creators');

const partners = [
	'SAC Brant',
	'Ganohkwasra Family Assault Support Services',
	'Grand Erie District School Board',
	'Victim Services of Brant',
	'Woodview Children’s Services',
	'St. Leonard’s (SOAR) Community Services',
	'Nova Vita Domestic Violence Prevention Services',
	'Brantford Police Services',
];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Our Story | Taylor the Turtle"
	description="How a classroom observation in 2010 grew into a community-built, provincially recognized child sexual abuse prevention program."
>
	<Header />
	<main id="main" class="paper">
		<div class="container-site py-14 lg:py-20">
			<h1 class="display-tight max-w-[20ch] text-4xl text-balance lg:text-5xl">Our Story</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 max-w-[52ch] text-forest/80">
				How a classroom observation in 2010 grew into a community-built, provincially recognized
				prevention program.
			</p>

			<section id="early-development" class="mt-14 scroll-mt-8" aria-labelledby="early-development-heading">
				<h2 id="early-development-heading" class="display-tight text-3xl text-balance lg:text-4xl">Early development</h2>
				<div class="mt-5 max-w-[65ch] space-y-5 text-forest/85 text-pretty">
					<p>
						Taylor the Turtle was created in 2010 in response to concerns about traditional child
						sexual abuse prevention programs that relied heavily on fear-based messaging and
						abstract “stranger danger” scenarios. While facilitating prevention sessions in an
						elementary school classroom, Program Founder Carrie Sinkowski observed that children
						struggled to understand scenario-based lessons and often became confused, distressed,
						or overly focused on literal details rather than safety concepts.
					</p>
					<p>
						Many commonly used “good touch/bad touch” programs were also found to be triggering
						for survivors, developmentally inappropriate for young children, and ineffective in
						reflecting how abuse most often occurs, typically within trusted relationships rather
						than through strangers.
					</p>
					<p>
						Taylor the Turtle was developed as a community-informed alternative grounded in
						children’s rights, body awareness, emotional literacy, and safety planning. Drawing on
						research, frontline experience with survivors, and feedback from educators, the
						program focuses on strengthening protective factors such as self-esteem, strong adult
						connections, and the ability to recognize and express feelings.
					</p>
					<p>
						Since its creation, Taylor the Turtle has been shaped through ongoing community input
						and has been delivered across schools and community settings. It was later recognized
						by the province as a best practice prevention initiative.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="creators" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-8" aria-labelledby="creators-heading">
				<h2 id="creators-heading" class="display-tight text-3xl text-balance lg:text-4xl">The creators</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 max-w-[60ch] text-forest/80">
					Taylor was brought to life by one family, working alongside their community colleagues.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-8 grid gap-6">
					{creators.map((person) => <PersonCard person={person} />)}
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="early-adoption" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-8" aria-labelledby="early-adoption-heading">
				<h2 id="early-adoption-heading" class="display-tight text-3xl text-balance lg:text-4xl">Early adoption</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 max-w-[60ch] text-forest/80">
					Taylor was developed with an advisory committee of eight community partners across
					Brantford, Brant County, and Six Nations.
				</p>
				<ul class="mt-8 grid max-w-[56rem] gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2" role="list">
					{partners.map((partner) => (
						<li class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-2xl bg-white px-5 py-4 font-bold text-forest">
							<span class="size-2.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-mustard" aria-hidden="true"></span>
							{partner}
						</li>
					))}
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="funding" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-8 rounded-3xl bg-sage-tile p-6 sm:p-8" aria-labelledby="funding-heading">
				<p class="text-[13px] font-extrabold tracking-[0.12em] text-pine uppercase">Funding acknowledgment</p>
				<h2 id="funding-heading" class="display-tight mt-2 max-w-[40ch] text-2xl text-balance">
					Funded by the Ministry of Children, Community and Social Services, Ontario’s Action Plan
					to End Gender-Based Violence.
				</h2>
				<div class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] space-y-4 text-forest/85 text-pretty">
					<p>
						This project is designed to expand and deliver child sexual abuse prevention
						programming to families, agencies, and sectors that interact with children. These
						groups will have the opportunity to participate in Taylor the Turtle, a now 16-year
						collaboration developed by eight community partners in the Brantford/Brant County and
						Six Nations communities under the leadership of the Sexual Assault Centre of Brant (SAC
						Brant) and Ganohkwasra Family Assault Support Services (Ganohkwasra).
					</p>
					<p>
						Taylor the Turtle trains Caring Adults to provide developmentally appropriate
						information and promote emotional literacy for young ones aged 18 months to six years
						and beyond. This dynamic program is built on Indigenous knowledge and the expertise
						developed over decades of sexual abuse prevention work and collective efforts to create
						a disclosure safe community.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</BaseLayout>
